--- body ---
## Context

Sweep IDs and model-set IDs in `experiments.toml` have accumulated
without a consistent naming axis. Problems:

- `[sweeps.census]` — name suggests statistical census; it is the
  main single-turn parametric sweep (terse one-liner prompt, no docs).
  Should align with the `parametric` method name from 0120.
- `[sweeps.decomposed]` — same misleading name as the method value;
  rename to match the chosen name from 0120 (e.g. `rag_categorical`).
- `[sets.rag]`, `[sets.sourced]` — model sets named after the sweep
  regime, not the model tier. Ambiguous as standalone identifiers.
- `[sets.ablation]` — marked "legacy alias" in a comment; remove.
- `[sets.decomposition_fix_probe]` — historical (ticket 0068 closed);
  remove or archive the set definition.
- `[sets.base_vs_census_extended]` — verbose; evaluate whether it can
  be collapsed into a named tier.
- `[sets.frontier_10labs]`, `[sets.frontier_3best]`, `[sets.frontier_cn]`
  — overlapping names without clear tier/scope hierarchy.

## Constraints

**TOML bare-key constraint:** TOML table headers cannot start with `-` or `+`.
Ablation sweep IDs must use underscores (e.g. `ablation_minus_persona`,
`ablation_plus_persona`) while the emitted `prompt_version` value uses
sign notation (`"-persona"`, `"+persona"`). The harness must translate.

## Actions

1. Audit every `[sweeps.*]` and `[sets.*]` key; classify each as
   clear / misleading / redundant / historical.
2. Propose renames aligned with the vocabulary from 0120.
3. Remove `[sets.ablation]` (legacy) and `[sets.decomposition_fix_probe]`
   (historical) after confirming no live sweep references them.
4. Apply renames in `experiments.toml`. Update any script that
   references sweep IDs by string (grep for sweep names in `src/`
   and `scripts/`).
5. Run `make test` green.

## Exit criteria

- No `[sweeps.census]` or `[sweeps.decomposed]` in `experiments.toml`.
- No legacy or historical set definitions remain.
- `make test` green.
- Unblocks 0122.
